from pathlib import Path
p=Path('PROTOTYPE-GUIDE.md');s=p.read_text();a=s.index('The private base has');b=s.index('\n\nSpend earned',a);s=s[:a]+'''The private base has a map altar, crafting workbench and bank chest. **Craft directly in your inventory:** right-click a material, choose Use, then click the equipment or map. Scroll of Wisdom identifies; Orb of Transmutation makes a normal item magic; Orb of Alchemy makes a normal/magic item rare; Chaos Orb rerolls modifiers; Exalted Orb adds a modifier; Vaal Orb corrupts. These have dedicated item IDs, names and original inventory icons. Their ground shapes currently reuse existing orb/paper cache models; fully custom 3D meshes remain future art work. P / Crafting is a reference and gem-upgrade panel, rather than the normal crafting workflow. P / Guide or Crafting can exchange old rune materials in your inventory for the new currencies.

Monster rewards land at the enemy's death tile and must be picked up. Equipment retains its exact identity and rolls, and full inventories leave loot on the ground. Private map loot remains until the instance closes, expires, or the player logs out. Uncollected loot is cleared with the instance. Starter kits and purchased recovery maps still go directly to inventory; those are grants rather than monster drops.

Corruption currently adds life implicits to equipment, up to two, and locks ordinary crafting. Advanced influence, enchants and broader corruption outcomes remain future content.'''+s[b:];s=s.replace('Spend earned passive points in P / Passives. Nodes require their parent.','Spend earned passive points in P / Passives. The connected graph branches from a central start: hover nodes for upgrades; bright outlines show available paths and gold marks allocated nodes. Nodes require their parent.');s=s.replace('Rewards overflow into the bank, then a saved mailbox claimed from Guide.','Non-loot grants can overflow into the bank, then a saved mailbox claimed from Guide.');p.write_text(s)
